{
  "name": "mame034",
  "title": "MAME 0.34 (DJGPP + Allegro 3 + SEAL, 1998)",
  "dir": "corpus/mame034",
  "fetch": "curl -Lo /tmp/mame034s.zip https://downloads.sourceforge.net/project/mame/mame/0.34/mame034s.zip && mkdir -p corpus/mame034 && (cd corpus/mame034 && unzip -qo /tmp/mame034s.zip)",
  "_doc": "MAME 0.34: the release that switched to CRC-32 for ROM integrity and finds a ROM inside a zip by its CRC whatever it is called. A jump of twenty-seven releases from 0.7: twelve CPU cores instead of one, hundreds of drivers, zip and PNG readers of its own.",
  "_units": "The makefile's OBJS and the members of every obj/*.a archive, in its order. Two ifdefs choose between an x86 assembly core and a C one: X86_ASM_68K (set in the makefile) and X86_ASM_6808 (commented out). Both are left unset here, which selects the makefile's own C alternatives -- the same choice as Quake's id386=0.",
